---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, breadcrumb } from '../data/site.ts';

const title = 'The Fasolati Platform — Products, Concepts & Research';
const description =
  'Explore Loria product information, the Lytica development concept, Gut Stack research and the proposed Life Board. Clear evidence gates before clinical claims.';

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    '@id': `${SITE}/platform/`,
    url: `${SITE}/platform/`,
    name: title,
    description,
    isPartOf: { '@id': `${SITE}/#website` },
    about: { '@id': `${SITE}/#organization` },
  },
  breadcrumb('Platform', '/platform/'),
];
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/platform/" schema={schema}>
  <div class="products-inner">
    <div class="p-hero">
      <h1>The Fasolati Platform</h1>
      <p>Oral care, gut-health research and a clearer view of systemic observations. One direction—with a separate evidence standard for every product, measurement and proposed action.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prod" id="p-lytica">
      <div class="prod-head"><h2 class="prod-name" style="color:var(--lytica)">Lytica</h2><span class="prod-badge" style="color:var(--lytica);border-color:var(--lytica)">Development Concept</span></div>
      <p class="prod-tagline">A staged approach to oral biofilm, designed to be tested.</p>
      <p class="prod-body">Lytica explores an enzyme-and-phage intervention concept. The development task is to define the finished formulation and delivery method, then evaluate safety and performance. The concept is not a prescription, an established clinical protocol or a promise of selective pathogen removal.</p>
      <div class="prod-mechs">
        <div class="prod-mech"><h4 style="color:var(--lytica)">Define the Intervention</h4><p>Specify the composition, exposure, delivery and intended use before assigning a result to Lytica. Candidate ingredients are not evidence that the combined product works.</p></div>
        <div class="prod-mech"><h4 style="color:var(--lytica)">Test the Finished Formulation</h4><p>Evaluate tolerability, local outcomes and analytical interference with an appropriate comparator. Any future systemic claim would need its own evidence.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="prod-body"><a href="/lytica/">Explore Lytica and request development updates →</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="prod" id="p-loria">
      <div class="prod-head"><h2 class="prod-name" style="color:var(--loria)">Loria</h2><span class="prod-badge" style="color:var(--loria);border-color:var(--loria)">Product Information</span></div>
      <p class="prod-tagline">An oral-care product deserves product-specific information.</p>
      <p class="prod-body">Ask about Loria’s current formulation, labeling, directions and purchasing details. We keep those questions separate from the broader research ambition: this page does not claim that Loria lowers bacterial vesicles or systemic inflammation, replaces prescribed care, or delivers benefits inferred from ingredient studies.</p>
      <div class="prod-mechs">
        <div class="prod-mech"><h4 style="color:var(--loria)">Know the Product</h4><p>Request information for the exact formulation and intended use. Follow its current labeling and discuss clinical questions with your dental professional.</p></div>
        <div class="prod-mech"><h4 style="color:var(--loria)">Keep Evidence in Scope</h4><p>Our product-development standard is to test the finished formulation rather than assemble an efficacy story from its ingredients.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="prod-body"><a href="/loria/">Loria product information and inquiries →</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="prod" id="p-fasolati-tier">
      <div class="prod-head"><h2 class="prod-name" style="color:var(--w)">Development & Collaboration</h2></div>
      <p class="prod-tagline">Clinical and consumer contexts need their own intended-use review.</p>
      <div class="tier-grid">
        <div class="tier" style="border-top-color:var(--maxoral)"><h4 style="color:var(--maxoral)">Maxoral</h4><span class="tier-badge" style="color:var(--maxoral)">Professional-Channel Concept</span><p>Maxoral is a proposed professional-channel direction. Formulations, intended uses and distribution arrangements require definition and review; no prescription classification or distribution partnership is asserted here.</p></div>
        <div class="tier" style="border-top-color:var(--fasolati-green)"><h4 style="color:var(--fasolati-green)">Fasolati</h4><span class="tier-badge" style="color:var(--fasolati-green)">Consumer-Facing Direction</span><p>The consumer-facing ambition is accessible product information and clearer evidence. A concept does not establish an OTC classification, a retail channel or a subscription offer.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="prod-body">Research-use and general-wellness guidance do not themselves classify a proposed assay, software feature or product claim. <a href="https://www.fda.gov/regulatory-information/search-fda-guidance-documents/distribution-in-vitro-diagnostic-products-labeled-research-use-only-or-investigational-use-only" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FDA research-use guidance</a> and <a href="https://www.fda.gov/regulatory-information/search-fda-guidance-documents/general-wellness-policy-low-risk-devices" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FDA general-wellness guidance</a> inform that review.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prod">
      <div class="prod-head"><h2 class="prod-name" style="color:var(--g)">Gut Stack</h2><span class="prod-badge" style="color:var(--g);border-color:var(--g)">Research & Development</span></div>
      <p class="prod-tagline">Ask when a gut-focused approach adds value—not assume it always does.</p>
      <p class="prod-body">The Gut Stack is a research direction for evaluating defined nutrition or microbiome interventions. Its components and benefits remain to be established. It is not a barrier-restoration protocol and is not matched to a personal gut-integrity score.</p>
      <p class="prod-body"><a href="/gut-stack/">Explore the Gut Stack direction →</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="prod">
      <div class="prod-head"><h2 class="prod-name" style="color:var(--t)">Fasolati Engine</h2><span class="prod-badge" style="color:var(--t);border-color:var(--t)">Life Board Development</span></div>
      <p class="prod-tagline">What changed? How confident are we? What next step is justified?</p>
      <p class="prod-body">The proposed Life Board would keep oral, gut and systemic observations distinct—not average them into a health score. Its design calls for visible measurement quality, uncertainty and supporting evidence, including the ability to say “not interpretable yet.” It is not a live clinical service or an autonomous prescribing system.</p>
      <div class="cascade">
        <div class="cascade-step"><span class="cascade-num" style="color:var(--t)">1</span><div class="cascade-content"><h4 style="color:var(--t)">Measure Before Interpreting</h4><p>Establish what the assay measures and how reliably it detects change.</p></div></div>
        <div class="cascade-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <div class="cascade-step"><span class="cascade-num" style="color:var(--t)">2</span><div class="cascade-content"><h4 style="color:var(--t)">Earn the Next Decision</h4><p>Test whether the result adds useful information and whether acting on it improves a meaningful outcome.</p></div></div>
      </div>
      <p class="prod-body"><a href="/science/#experiments">Read the proposed experiments in the Science Spine →</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <nav class="page-next" aria-label="Related pages">
    <a href="/shop/"><h3>Products & Concepts</h3><p>Explore the portfolio and product-information paths.</p></a>
    <a href="/science/"><h3>Science Spine</h3><p>The evidence, limitations and proposed validation work.</p></a>
    <a href="/partner/"><h3>Partner With Us</h3><p>Discuss research, clinical and commercial questions.</p></a>
  </nav>
</Base>
